https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40284823","site":"Hacker News","score":537,"comments":351,"year":2024},{"title":"Backyard Coffee and Jazz in Kyoto","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44356248","site":"Hacker News","score":596,"comments":269,"year":2025},{"title":"Be careful with that thing, it's a confidential coffee maker","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=31168150","site":"Hacker News","score":635,"comments":204,"year":2022},{"title":"Distributor cancelled an order and we need to move 30k bags of coffee [updated]","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=34186886","site":"Hacker News","score":402,"comments":368,"year":2022},{"title":"Civet coffee: why it's time to cut the crap","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=6386232","site":"Hacker News","score":575,"comments":194,"year":2013},{"title":"Add coffee stains to LaTeX documents (2021)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39316193","site":"Hacker News","score":501,"comments":140,"year":2024},{"title":"Coffee naps are better than coffee or naps alone","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=8239251","site":"Hacker News","score":470,"comments":161,"year":2014},{"title":"Chinese green tea is bringing people together in West Africa, 3 cups at a time","url":"https://news.abolish.capital/post/72956","site":"Lemmy · china","score":4,"comments":0,"year":2026}],"web":[{"title":"Green tea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_tea"},{"title":"Caffeine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caffeine"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Facial fat & puffiness","chain":["Caffeine and green tea polyphenols","Mild diuretic, vasoconstrictor effect","Less puffy face"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Coffee and green tea are drunk as a morning routine for a mild diuretic effect that users hope leaves the face less puffy. Both contain caffeine, green tea adds polyphenols such as EGCG, and the effect on the face has not been studied."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The coffee or green tea ritual refers to drinking caffeinated beverages as part of a routine aimed at reducing facial puffiness or improving appearance. Both beverages contain caffeine, and green tea also contains polyphenols such as EGCG [1][2].","Caffeine can briefly increase urine output after large single doses in people not accustomed to it, but regular users develop tolerance [2]. Wikipedia reports that green tea polyphenols have no proven biological effects in humans and that health claims were not supported by sufficient evidence in a 2011 EFSA review [1]. No studies found on drinking either beverage to reduce facial puffiness."],"infobox":[["Type","Dietary habit"],["Active compounds","Caffeine; EGCG (green tea)"],["EFSA caffeine guidance","Up to 400 mg/day for non-pregnant adults [2]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Practitioners drink coffee or green tea, often in the morning, in the belief that caffeine or tea antioxidants reduce water retention or improve skin. Green tea originated in China and spread across East Asia [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found on drinking coffee or green tea for facial puffiness. General green tea research reports small blood pressure reductions and lower cholesterol in a 2013 Cochrane analysis, but no good evidence for weight loss, and no significant effect on C-reactive protein in a 2015 meta-analysis [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Safety","paras":["EFSA considers up to 400 mg of caffeine per day not a safety concern for non-pregnant adults, and 200 mg for pregnant or lactating women. Caffeine can delay sleep, and doses as low as 100 mg per day may disrupt sleep in some people [2]. High-dose green tea extracts have been linked to liver toxicity, and Health Canada recommended a warning label in 2017; traditionally brewed tea is considered safe by EFSA with rare liver damage [1]."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Green tea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_tea","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Caffeine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caffeine","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Green tea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_tea","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"coffee and cig for breakfast","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-and-cig-for-breakfast.1775511/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260220135647/https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-and-cig-for-breakfast.1775511/"},{"title":"Coffee is the worst thing you can drink","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-the-worst-thing-you-can-drink.1562085/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250915061248/https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-the-worst-thing-you-can-drink.1562085/"},{"title":"Coffee is a hard looksmin.","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-a-hard-looksmin.1525590/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250809084403/https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-a-hard-looksmin.1525590/"},{"title":"coffee is poison","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-poison.1401088/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250519113733/https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-poison.1401088/"},{"title":"coffee is very good for your thyroid","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-very-good-for-your-thyroid.626184/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221220075227/https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-very-good-for-your-thyroid.626184/"},{"title":"coffee is so good for leanmaxxing","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-so-good-for-leanmaxxing.509801/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220614034044/https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-so-good-for-leanmaxxing.509801/"},{"title":"coffee is being a cuck on tc","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coffee-is-being-a-cuck-on-t